<!-- TODO(jess): review and set published: true when this is your voice. -->

Behind the scenes I've been building out the actual membership system: someone applies, a keyholder reviews it and can schedule a tour, a decision gets made, and if it's a yes the person gets provisioned in. Alongside that, a way to track contributions (cash, check, or Stripe in test mode) with append-only receipts, so the record can't quietly change after the fact.

Every piece of this has been built against a real Postgres database and put through hostile testing on purpose: replayed webhooks, forged tokens, double-claims, race conditions between two keyholders acting at once. It's held up so far, through a couple of rounds of edits.

None of it is live. Most of it is already merged and reviewed — what's left is waiting on one more thing: the actual words. What the application form says, what the keyholder roles are called, what the agreement text is, that's mine to write. Once that's in hand this ships.
